  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowered Maya Tseltal women fostering food security and diversified, sustainable smallholder agriculture in Chiln, Chiapas.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tseltal indigenous women and their families struggle to obtain sufficient food through small-scale agriculture. At the IAF, we support community-led solutions that enhance food security in Mexico. In Chiln, Chiapas, our grantee partner, Sbelal Kuxlejalil A.C. (SKU) provide Tseltal women with technical assistance for sustainable vegetable, fruit and small livestock production to improve their livelihoods. In addition to improving food security, SKUs activities strengthen grassroots organizations and empower Tseltal women as community leaders.</narrative>
  </description>
